    {
      "id": "MocKGnZ28oTeLlrbdsqOk",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -947.1666666666661,
      "y": -572.452380952381,
      "width": 2402.144000000001,
      "height": 437.28736717827627,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ac",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1390219102,
      "version": 655,
      "versionNonce": 1768322755,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790785264877,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "System design is the process of choosing and organizing the right components, technologies, and architecture to build a\nlarge-scale application that works reliably, efficiently, and smoothly.\n\nIt involves deciding things like:\n\nHow different components communicate with each other\nHow data is stored and accessed\nHow the system handles many users\nHow the application remains reliable and scalable",
      "fontSize": 38.86998819362456,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "System design is the process of choosing and organizing the right components, technologies, and architecture to build a large-scale application that works reliably, efficiently, and smoothly.\n\nIt involves deciding things like:\n\nHow different components communicate with each other\nHow data is stored and accessed\nHow the system handles many users\nHow the application remains reliable and scalable",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "gnj8AjcsNo7jp1iPJPPDy",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -887.1666666666663,
      "y": 305.8809523809523,
      "width": 1089.6440000000011,
      "height": 680.2247933884297,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "acV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1742148738,
      "version": 833,
      "versionNonce": 1804641891,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790785264877,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Low-Level Design focuses on designing the internal\nstructure of a specific feature or part of an application.\n\nIn an interview, the interviewer might ask you to design\na particular feature, and you need to explain how you\nwould approach and implement it.\n\nFor example:\n\nDesigning a parking lot system\nDesigning a payment system\nDesigning a notification feature\nDeciding which classes, objects, methods, and\nrelationships are needed",
      "fontSize": 38.86998819362456,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Low-Level Design focuses on designing the internal structure of a specific feature or part of an application.\n\nIn an interview, the interviewer might ask you to design a particular feature, and you need to explain how you would approach and implement it.\n\nFor example:\n\nDesigning a parking lot system\nDesigning a payment system\nDesigning a notification feature\nDeciding which classes, objects, methods, and relationships are needed",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "DB-xQcJwoIqm5ps9qYjec",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 312.8333333333337,
      "y": 304.21428571428567,
      "width": 1089.6440000000011,
      "height": 437.28736717827627,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "acl",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 265556382,
      "version": 942,
      "versionNonce": 1947460099,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790785264877,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "High-Level Design focuses on designing the architecture\nof an entire application or system.\n\nIn an interview, you might be asked to design a large\napplication such as YouTube, WhatsApp, or an e-\ncommerce platform.\n\nYou would discuss components such as: Servers , Load ,\nbalancers , Databases , Caches and etc..",
      "fontSize": 38.86998819362456,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "High-Level Design focuses on designing the architecture of an entire application or system.\n\nIn an interview, you might be asked to design a large application such as YouTube, WhatsApp, or an e-commerce platform.\n\nYou would discuss components such as: Servers , Load , balancers , Databases , Caches and etc..",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
